QuestGuidance.Register("en",79,{
[2497]="700375C9\n1\tTalk to Fríthbert\030Talk to Edhild\tFríthbert and Edhild are with their nurse, Engifu, at Fríthild's house, east of the Mead Hall of Stoke. Reeve Fríthild asked you to visit her children, Fríthbert and Edhild, and give them words of comfort and encouragement.\n",
[2498]="700669B1\n1\tCollect barrels of black powder (total: 3)\tIgerna has asked you to gather barrels of the goblins' black powder. Barrels can be found in the camp outside, as well as inside, the cave at Krauzhaf, in Pinnath Gelin.\n2\tBlow up the south-western tunnel\tWith a hefty supply of dangerously explosive barrels of black powder, you are ready to seal off some of the goblins' tunnels. You should start with the south-western tunnel, in the cave in Pinnath Gelin.\n3\tBlow up the western tunnel\tThe black powder did a fine job of blocking the south-western tunnel. You should move on to the western tunnel and blow that one up as well. The western tunnel is in the Krauzhaf cave in Pinnath Gelin.\n4\tBlow up the north-western tunnel\tWith both the western and south-western tunnels blocked, you have but one left. You should blow up the north-western tunnel in the Krauzhaf cave in Pinnath Gelin.\n5\tSpeak to Igerna outside the cave\tYou have battled your way through Krauzhaf and blown up the three tunnels that the Ronkrúm goblins were using to crawl out of the mountain. Igerna is waiting to speak with you outside the Krauzhaf cave, in Pinnath Gelin.\n",
[2499]="70071625\n1\tDefeat Overseer Basóra\030Defeat Overseer Purjóro\030Defeat Overseer Jóha\tThe Ordâkhai overseers have arrived to attempt to regain control of the Esh Mêkag pit-mine. You should defeat Overseer Basóra, Overseer Purjóro, and Overseer Jóha.\n2\tTalk to Ebuzâm\tYou have done much to aid the thralls revolting in Esh Mêkag. You should return to Ebuzâm.\n",
[2500]="7002BCD5\n1\tTalk to Andras\tThe escaped prisoner is at the Ox-clan merchant camp in Nan Curunír. Mabon has asked you to take him to meet the prisoner who escaped from Orthanc to learn if he knows whether his father, Andras, yet lives.\n2\tTalk to Mabon\tMabon is at the Ox-clan camp outside of Isengard in Nan Curunír. You should speak with Mabon at once.\n",
[2501]="7003EA74\n1\tCollect bear-pelts on the High Moor (total: 6)\tBears can be found throughout the High Moor, in the Trollshaws. Canaddal has asked you to hunt bears for their pelts.\n2\tBring the bear-pelts to Canaddal\tCanaddal is posted at the head of the path leading down to the Bruinen Gorges from the High Moor. You should bring the bear-pelts you collected to Canaddal.\n",
[2502]="7002C467\n1\tSearch for Byrnstan's stolen rations\tThe stolen rations can likely be found hidden somewhere in Stangard. You should try to recover the stolen rations for Byrnstan, so that he does not go hungry.\n2\tRecover the stolen rations (quantity: see journal)\tThe stolen rations are in the kennels of Stangard. Someone in Stangard stole rations from the lock-house; this food should be recovered, and the thief identified.\n3\tConfront Athulf, the owner of the dogs, for his crime\t\n4\tBring the rations to Byrnstan and plead Athulf's cause\tByrnstan can be found guarding the door to the Mead Hall. You should plead Athulf's cause to Byrnstan.\n5\tTalk to Gadda about what transpired\tGadda can be found near the Mead Hall in Stangard. You should speak with Gadda about the food being so scarce that it drives men to steal.\n",
[2503]="7005A67A\n1\tExamine the broken mirror trap\tThe broken mirror trap can be found at Shalakibal, in eastern Máttugard. You should find and assess the broken mirror trap.\n2\tFind the large mirror shard\030Find the small mirror shard\030Find the mirror trap lever\030Find the mirror trap gear\tParts for the mirror trap can be found scattered throughout Shalakibal. You should search for parts to fix the broken mirror trap.\n3\tRepair the broken mirror trap\tThe broken mirror trap can be found at Shalakibal, in eastern Máttugard. You should attempt to repair the broken mirror trap.\n4\tContinue repairing the broken mirror trap\tThe broken mirror trap can be found at Shalakibal, in eastern Máttugard. You should attempt to repair the broken mirror trap.\n5\tCompleted\tRepaired the broken mirror trap.\n",
[2504]="7001A4AE\n1\tTalk to Prestadír at the Haunted Inn\tPrestadír is at the Haunted Inn, east from Echad Mothelen. Mothelen suggested you speak with Prestadír to learn more about the shades of the Dourstocks.\n",
[2505]="70044118\n1\tDefend terrified soldiers from Orcs and rouse subjugated soldiers\tYou should defend the terrified soldiers and rouse subjugated soldiers before they can attempt to open the Great Gate.\n",
[2506]="700442DB\n1\tDefend terrified soldiers from Orcs and rouse subjugated soldiers\tYou should defend the terrified soldiers and rouse subjugated soldiers before they can attempt to open the Great Gate.\n",
[2507]="7002BFFD\n1\tCollect light blue medallions (total: 6)\tKhundolar sorcerers can be found throughout the Brown Lands and at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands. Céola has asked you to find some of the other medallions his scouts reported seeing.\n2\tBring the light blue medallions to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg. You should bring the medallions you found to Céola.\n",
[2508]="7002BFFC\n1\tCollect dark blue medallions (total: 6)\tKhundolar sorcerers can be found throughout the Brown Lands and at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands. Céola has asked you to find some of the other medallions his scouts reported seeing.\n2\tBring the dark blue medallions to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg. You should bring the medallions you found to Céola.\n",
[2509]="70044D67\n1\tComplete Quest: The Southern Great Guest-house\030Complete Quest: Merethrond\tIorlas is guarding the rise to the Seventh Circle. Beregond is at the Citadel. You should speak with Iorlas and Beregond.\n2\tSpeak with Ormatar\tOrmatar can be found at the Citadel. You should speak with Ormatar.\n3\tFind the source of the scuffle on the Prow\tThe Prow is near the Citadel. Find the source of the scuffle on the Prow.\n4\tGet between Iorlas and Beregond\tThe Prow is near the Citadel. Stop Beregond and Iorlas from fighting.\n5\tHear what Iorlas has to say\tThe Prow is near the Citadel. Speak with Iorlas on the Prow.\n6\tHear what Beregond has to say\tThe Prow is near the Citadel. Speak with Beregond on the Prow.\n7\tHear what Iorlas has to say\tThe Prow is near the Citadel. Speak with Iorlas on the Prow.\n8\tHear what Beregond has to say\tThe Prow is near the Citadel. Speak with Beregond on the Prow.\n9\tSpeak to Ormatar and cover for the brothers\tOrmatar can be found at the Citadel. You should speak to with Ormatar.\n",
[2510]="7005983C\n1\tDefeat Brundurch the Great Boar\tBrundurch the Great Boar can be found in the northern Wildwood. Linnet has asked you to defeat the maddened boar, Brundurch.\n2\tTalk to Linnet\tLinnet is located in central Wildwood. You should talk to Linnet Redholm.\n",
[2511]="7004A819\n1\tDefeat Thorakó's Warriors (total: 6)\030Destroy cages (total: 10)\tIngold has asked you to defeat Olog-hai and destroy cages in Fushaum Tûm.\n",
[2512]="700509C1\n1\tDefeat Bráthadan, Scourge of Óinsbridge\tBráthadan poses a great threat to all that enter Óinsbridge.\n2\tDefeat Bráthadan, Scourge of Óinsbridge\tBráthadan poses a great threat to all that enter Óinsbridge.\n3\tCompleted\tBráthadan poses a great threat to all that enter Óinsbridge.\n",
[2513]="70035059\n1\tSouth-west of Gárnoth's Farm rumour is spreading around town is that there are clues of Brúlk's return. Look for footprints or a half-eaten animal corpse that appears to be from a very large Warg.\t\n2\tReturn to Ebba in Forlaw\tThe widow Ebba awaits your return in her late husband's home in Forlaw.\n",
[2514]="7005A99D\n1\tStomp the grodbog grubs\tGrodbog grubs can be found at Brúvraum in western Máttugard. You should stomp the grodbog grubs.\n2\tStomp the grodbog grubs (total: 12)\tGrodbog grubs can be found at Brúvraum in western Máttugard. You should stomp the grodbog grubs.\n",
[2515]="7005A996\n1\tBurn the poisonous mushrooms\tPoisonous mushrooms can be found at Brúvraum in western Máttugard. You should burn the poisonous mushrooms.\n2\tBurn the poisonous mushrooms (total: 12)\tPoisonous mushrooms can be found at Brúvraum in western Máttugard. You should burn the poisonous mushrooms.\n",
[2516]="70007950\n1\tBring toolbox to Builder Earur\030Collect Builder Earur's toolbox\tBuilder Earur's cart was overturned south of Archet, near the gate to Combe. Builder Earur is in Archet, north of the overturned cart. Builder Earur has asked you to recover the toolbox he left in the wreckage of his cart, overturned by a mad boar south of Archet.\n",
[2517]="70046A18\n1\tSpeak with the Master of Apprentices\tYou should find a Master of Apprentices willing to take on pupils in Combe. Builder Earur directed you to a crafting master in Combe. He mentioned that the master can be found by following the left path once you enter Combe centre.\n",
[2518]="7006EC22\n1\tBuild sand-castles on the beach (total: 4)\tYou have accepted a commission to construct four sand-castles on the beach to add to the festive atmosphere.\n2\tTalk to Merkhâma\tYou have fulfilled your obligation to build sand-castles on Furtherholm's beaches. You should return to Merkhâma outside of The Cracked Flagon to get your reward.\n",
[2519]="7000C73B\n1\tBring the work order to Nan Henwood\tNan Henwood is near the gates of the Bree homestead, south-east of Sarabeth Lowbanks, east of the old ruins there. Sarabeth Lowbanks has asked you to deliver a work order confirmation to Nan Henwood.\n2\tBring the work order to Bill Twiggins\tBill Twiggins is in the market square of the Bree homestead. Nan Henwood has signed the work order and asked you to take it to Bill Twiggins.\n",
[2520]="7000C739\n1\tBring the work order to Barchiril\tBarchiril is near the gates of the Duillond homestead, across the river and south from the cross-road. Badennas has asked you to deliver a work order confirmation to Barchiril.\n2\tBring the work order to Barthavron\tBarthavron is in the market square of the Duillond community. Barchiril has signed the work order and asked you to take it to Barthavron.\n",
[2521]="70026E52\n1\tCollect kindling for the bonfire (total: 6)\030Pick scented herbs (total: 3)\tKindling and scented herbs can be collected on the stark and rough plains around Lhan Tarren. You should collect herbs and kindling for a magnificent bonfire to be lit at the festival.\n2\tBring the kindling and scented herbs to Ivor\tIvor awaits you in Lhan Tarren, the Stag-clan's village of Dunland. You should bring the kindling and scented herbs you gathered to Ivor, who wishes to use them to fuel an especially magnificent bonfire.\n",
[2522]="700304B7\n1\tDefeat Easterling workers in the Woodyard (total: 8)\tThe Woodyard is on the eastern side of Jóshkhin Orda in the Wold, to the north of North-torr. You should defeat Easterling workers in the Woodyard to cease the construction of deadly siege-weapons.\n2\tCompleted\tThe Easterlings who build the weapons of war are as deadly as those who wield the weapons. You have defeated many of these builders, preventing more siege-craft from being assembled for the assault on the Rohirrim.\n",
[2523]="7000C73A\n1\tBring the work order to Andy Brockhouse\tAndy Brockhouse is near the gates of the Michel Delving homestead, south of the town proper. The woodworker in Overhill has asked you to deliver a work order confirmation to Andy Brockhouse.\n2\tBring the work order to Rolf Bracegirdle\tRolf Bracegirdle is in the market square of the Michel Delving homestead. Andy Brockhouse has signed the work order and asked you to take it to Rolf Bracegirdle.\n",
[2524]="7000E399\n1\tTrade with Ofráth\030Collect Moose-antler\tOfráth can be found along the road south of Kauppa-kohta. Eija has asked you to go to the dwarves and trade a set of antlers for a satchel of salt to help in the hide-curing process.\n2\tUse the curing barrel\tThe curing barrel is next to Eija in Kauppa-kohta's shoreline sled-building camp. Now that you have obtained a satchel of salt from the dwarves, you should return to Eija and place it in the curing barrel.\n3\tTalk to Eija\tEija is in Kauppa-kohta's sled-building camp, at the lake's eastern shore. Having started the curing process for the rawhide, you should speak with Eija once more.\n",
[2525]="7000C738\n1\tBring the work order to Rúni\tRúni is near the gates of the Thorin's Hall homestead, west of Thorin's Gate. Nagli has asked you to take a work order to Rúni..\n2\tBring the work order to Rambi\tRambi is in the market square of the Thorin's Hall homestead. Rúni has signed the work order and asked you to take it to Rambi.\n",
[2526]="70058CF4\n1\tCollect thick branches (total: 10)\tThick branches can be found fallen from the trees in Elderslade. Dúghild has asked you to collect thick branches in Elderslade.\n2\tDeliver the thick branches to Dúghild\tDúghild can be found at Khadâsh-gâra in Elderslade. You have collected a number of thick branches in Elderslade and should now deliver them to Dúghild at Khadâsh-gâra.\n",
[2527]="7000D81A\n1\tCollect clover (total: 5)\tThe Greenfields are north of Brockenborings in the Shire. Sigismond North-took has asked that you collect clover used for making Bullroarer's Brew.\n2\tTalk to Sigismond North-took\030Collect Clover (total: 5)\tSigismond North-took is in Brockenborings, south of the Greenfields. You should bring the clover you collected to Sigismond North-took.\n",
[2528]="7000D85B\n1\tToast to Bandobras's Health\tThe Challenge Field is located just east of Brockenborings. To participate in the Bullroarer's Challenge, Tobias Brockhouse told you to stand on the starting platform, pick up your official Bullroarer's Challenge brew tankard, toast to Bandobras's health, and make it across the fence to the other platform, where Belgo is standing, before time runs out. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Sigismond North-took\tSigismond North-took is in Brockenborings. Speak with Sigismond North-took to claim your prize.\n",
})
